BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Honoring the Red Rocks: Bird Gathering at Tlaquepaque
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261107
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261108
DTSTAMP:20261104T184806Z
UID:47d03a0ea824760e37355bdf@visitarizona-calendar
DESCRIPTION:### First of its kind in Sedona Celebrate Native American Heri
 tage Month in Sedona with Honoring the Red Rocks\, a special cultural gath
 ering featuring traditional Native American bird singing\, bird dancing\, 
 and Yavapai storytelling at Tlaquepaque Arts & Shopping Village. Experienc
 e the living traditions of Arizona's Indigenous communities as bird singer
 s and dancers from across the region share songs\, stories\, and cultural 
 expressions passed down through generations. This first-of-its-kind gather
 ing in Sedona honors the cultural significance of the area's iconic red ro
 cks while celebrating the rich heritage and shared traditions of Yavapai a
 nd Yuman-speaking peoples. Visitors can enjoy traditional bird songs and d
 ances featuring AshaaTakook\, Wali & Kynoe\, the Red Mountain Group\, the 
 Parker Boys\, and Michael Mirelez & Desert Cahuilla Bird. Salt Singer Matt
 hew Cruz will also participate\, alongside an honored Yavapai Elder who wi
 ll share traditional storytelling and cultural knowledge. Set within the p
 icturesque courtyards of Tlaquepaque\, this welcoming community gathering 
 offers an opportunity to connect with Indigenous culture\, learn about the
  significance of Native traditions\, and experience the enduring relations
 hip between the Yavapai people and Sedona's red rock landscape. **Event De
 tails** * _`Saturday\, November 7\, 2026`_ * _`Time: 11 a.m.–4 p.m.`_ * 
 _`Tlaquepaque Arts & Shopping Village\, Patio del Norte`_ * _`336 State Ro
 ute 179\, Sedona\, AZ 86336`_ * _`Free and open to the public`_ * _`Tradit
 ional bird singing\, bird dancing\, Yavapai storytelling\, and cultural ex
 change`_ * _`Contact:`_[_`waldinefox@gmail.com`_](https://waldinefox@gmail
 .com/) All are welcome to attend\, and traditional bird singers and dancer
 s are encouraged to participate. Join the celebration and experience the s
 ongs\, stories\, and living cultural traditions that honor Sedona's Indige
 nous heritage and the enduring spirit of the Red Rocks. ![Image 46](https:
 //cdn.prod.website-files.com/683a4969614808c01cd0d378/6ae8d16d93b4817354ce
 787c_image.png.png)\n\nEvent website: https://hualapai-nsn.gov/\n\nVisit A
 rizona listing: https://www.visitarizona.com/events/honoring-the-red-rocks
 -bird-gathering-at-tlaquepaque
LAST-MODIFIED:20261104T184806Z
LOCATION:Tlaquepaque Arts & Shopping Village\, Patio del Norte
URL:https://www.visitarizona.com/events/honoring-the-red-rocks-bird-gather
 ing-at-tlaquepaque
END:VEVENT
